# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in every checkout.
#
# Why pin it: a CRLF shell script is a hard failure on POSIX — a CRLF `set -eu`
# raises "set: -: invalid option" (measured on .githooks/pre-push, which was
# checked out CRLF by core.autocrlf=true and then refused to run under sh).
# Hooks, tools/*.sh and the CI steps are shared between this Windows dev machine
# and Linux CI, so the whole tree is normalized instead of chasing exceptions.
# text=auto keeps binary files (images, .tgz, font programs) untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
